"""Short Python Tasks: 100 single-turn prompts where all three coding-style features can fire.

Every task (a) builds a list from a collection, so a comprehension or a for-loop with append are
both natural; (b) needs string literals (keys, labels, separators), so quote style shows; and
(c) mentions input that can be missing or malformed, so error handling (try/except vs
assert/raise) is a live choice. The prompts never ask for a style. Written for this repo; the
paper's own 100 tasks are not released.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

SUFFIX = "\n\nReply with the complete function in a single Python code block."

